scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:1011:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca-423-2000-f-22.1.2019.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca-423-2000-f-22.1.2019.pdf,,COA,2019,A person who claims prescriptive title against the rightful owner who has the paper title has a very heavy burden to prove all the requirements prescribed in section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance.,A person who claims prescriptive title against the rightful owner who has the paper title has a very heavy burden to prove all the requirements prescribed in section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance.,SRC071-s3,none,section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:1023:draftly-rule-courts-coa-CA-RII-0001-23.pdf-1,courts-coa-CA-RII-0001-23.pdf,,COA,,It is too late in the day to challenge the district court’s order on substitution both in law and facts.,Hence the application of the substituted 01st defendant petitioner is dismissed with costs.,SRC030-s394(2),bad-source,section 394(2) of the Civil Procedure Code,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:1034:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_1187_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_1187_98.pdf,,COA,,"A party can make submissions on the devolution of title of the parties to the action even at the appeal stage, and the court may order a re-trial if necessary.","Merely because her claim was to have an exclusion of a particular portion of the corpus, she is not prevented from taking up the matters pertaining to the devolution of title of the parties to the action even at this appeal stage.",SRC030-s25,ok,Section 25 of the Partition Act,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_cleaned.csv:1039:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_242_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_242_99.pdf,,COA,,"A party invoking the provisions of section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance to defeat the ownership of an adverse claimant to immovable property must establish a starting point for their acquisition of prescriptive rights, which must be undisturbed, uninterrupted, adverse to or independent of that of the former possessor and must have lasted for at least ten years.","According to section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance such a possession must be undisturbed, uninterrupted, adverse to or independent of that of the former possessor and should have lasted for at least ten years before he could transform such possession into prescriptive title.",SRC071-s3,ok-unchecked,section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
