scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:436:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-47-1,commonlii-LKCA-2000-47,(2001) 2 Sri LR 371,LKCA,2000,A mere deviation in a contractual term does not negate the whole contract unless the parties intended to terminate it.,"(i) Increase of rentals did not result in a new contract. A mere deviation with regard to a term in the original contractual document need not negate the whole document unless parties intended to terminate the contract set out therein - Negotiating an increased rent does not give rise to a new contract but merely result in the variation of one term of the contract. Per Wigneswaran J., ""Courts are fast making use of technical grounds and traversing of procedural guidelines to dispose of cases without reaching out to 372 the core of the matters in issue and ascertain the truth to bring justice to the litigants. This tendency is most unfortunate. It could boomerang on the judiciary as well as the existing judicial system.""",SRC030-s150,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:463:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-9-1,commonlii-LKCA-2000-9,(2001) 2 Sri LR 355,LKCA,2000,A plaintiff can file a new action at any time during the proceedings of a previous action.,"(i) The Plaint in the present case was filed on 2.1.1984 nearly an year after institution of the divorce action and four days before the answer was filed in the divorce action. Nothing in law barred, the Plaintiff from filing such an action. (ii) The failure to seek relief to enforce forfeiture in the Divorce Action cannot therefore be held to have operated as Res Judicata against him. The Defendant has reserved his rights to enforce forfeiture separately when he filed his answer. This is in accordance with the law and there was no question of Res Judicata affecting his rights. Wigneswaran J., ""It was the duty of the Judge in the first instance to have raised the issues. According to practice",SRC030-s146(2),none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:464:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-9-2,commonlii-LKCA-2000-9,(2001) 2 Sri LR 355,LKCA,2000,A party's failure to seek relief to enforce forfeiture in a previous action does not operate as Res Judicata against them.,"(i) The Plaint in the present case was filed on 2.1.1984 nearly an year after institution of the divorce action and four days before the answer was filed in the divorce action. Nothing in law barred, the Plaintiff from filing such an action. (ii) The failure to seek relief to enforce forfeiture in the Divorce Action cannot therefore be held to have operated as Res Judicata against him. The Defendant has reserved his rights to enforce forfeiture separately when he filed his answer. This is in accordance with the law and there was no question of Res Judicata affecting his rights. Wigneswaran J., ""It was the duty of the Judge in the first instance to have raised the issues. According to practice",SRC030-s146(2),none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:465:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2001-1-1,commonlii-LKCA-2001-1,(2002) 2 Sri LR 384,LKCA,2001,A party's prescription of land is determined by the land's physical boundaries as seen from the land itself.,"The appellant has prescribed to the land as seen from - (1) Continued possession of the corpus after the death of E and from 1969 after the widow left the corpus. (2) Planting with coconuts, etc., and enjoying the produce. (3) Friends and relations arranging a marriage in 1970, with the marriage ceremony being taken in the house and premises in suit. (4) The widow of E not attending the marriage ceremony. (5) Building extensions, effecting repairs, renting a portion of the house in 1970. 385 (6) Continued possession after marriage. (7) Payment of rates and taxes from 1973. (8) Long and undisturbed possession of the corpus been corroborated by the evidence of the Grama Sevaka",SRC071-s3,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
