scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:686:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2004-51-1,commonlii-LKCA-2004-51,(2004) 2 Sri LR 97,LKCA,2004,The relevance of a fact under section 2 is determined by what is relevant.,"(1) What is relevant under section 2(4) C is not whether the plaintiff himself occupied the relevant premises on. 01.01.1980, as its owner but whether the premises were occupied on that day by its owner (whether it be the plaintiff or not is immaterial) or by a tenant",SRC028-s2(4),none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
