scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:154:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-39-1,commonlii-LKCA-1986-39,(1986) 1 Sri LR 378,LKCA,1986,"In a vindicatory suit the plaintiff must prove his title. Having failed to prove his own title, he cannot rely on the weakness of the 1st defendant's title. Whatever the strength of the 1st defendant's case, if the plaintiff fails to establish his title, plaintiff's case must necessarily fail","In a vindicatory suit the plaintiff must prove his title. Having failed to prove his own title, he cannot rely on the weakness of the 1st defendant's title. Whatever the strength of the 1st defendant's case, if the plaintiff fails to establish his title, plaintiff's case must necessarily fail",SRC071-s3,none,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:155:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-1-1,commonlii-LKCA-1987-1,(1987) 2 Sri LR 78,LKCA,1987,A co-owner can sue his neighbour also a co-owner of the adjacent land for definition of boundaries but he takes a risk because even if he is successful the decree in his favour will not bind the other co-owners of the adjacent land,"(1) A co-owner can sue his neighbour also a co-owner of the adjacent land for definition of boundaries but he takes a risk because even if he is successful the decree in his favour will not bind the other co-owners of the adjacent land. (2) The burden of proving the essential facts in a suit for definition of boundaries is on the plaintiff. (3) In the guise of an action for definition of boundaries a plaintiff cannot vindicate title to an encroachment. 79 (4) From the age of the existing fence trees on the Western boundary of Lot A the undisputed claim before the surveyor by the defendant of the three 25-year old coconut trees and the failure of the plaintiff to complain immediately to a person in authority when in 1946 he found barbed wire strands removed from his barbed wire fence, the plaintiff must be held to have failed to establish the r equisites of an action for definition of boundaries. He has failed to show that there did exist e prior live or other physical boundary fence along the eastern boundary of Lot A as claimed by him. Further in the guise of having his eastern boundary defined the plaintiff was in fact seeking to have himself declared entitled to Lot A. (5) Because of the failure of the plaintiff to produce the plan of 1879 and prove the plan of 1973 the correctness of Dharmawardena's plan No. 823 is also in doubt",SRC030-s18,none,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules.csv:156:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-1-2,commonlii-LKCA-1987-1,(1987) 2 Sri LR 78,LKCA,1987,The burden of proving the essential facts in a suit for definition of boundaries is on the plaintiff,"(1) A co-owner can sue his neighbour also a co-owner of the adjacent land for definition of boundaries but he takes a risk because even if he is successful the decree in his favour will not bind the other co-owners of the adjacent land. (2) The burden of proving the essential facts in a suit for definition of boundaries is on the plaintiff. (3) In the guise of an action for definition of boundaries a plaintiff cannot vindicate title to an encroachment. 79 (4) From the age of the existing fence trees on the Western boundary of Lot A the undisputed claim before the surveyor by the defendant of the three 25-year old coconut trees and the failure of the plaintiff to complain immediately to a person in authority when in 1946 he found barbed wire strands removed from his barbed wire fence, the plaintiff must be held to have failed to establish the r equisites of an action for definition of boundaries. He has failed to show that there did exist e prior live or other physical boundary fence along the eastern boundary of Lot A as claimed by him. Further in the guise of having his eastern boundary defined the plaintiff was in fact seeking to have himself declared entitled to Lot A. (5) Because of the failure of the plaintiff to produce the plan of 1879 and prove the plan of 1973 the correctness of Dharmawardena's plan No. 823 is also in doubt",SRC030-s18,none,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
