+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1985-57-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court itself held on appeal that R2, having been admitted without objection at trial, could not then be objected to."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1985-58-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The point was ratio, but the statement omits the material context that the duty was to specify the party and deadline for registering lis pendens under section 19(2)(b)."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1985-58-2","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The judgment decided a belated lis pendens application in a partition action, not a general rule that parties must comply with statutory requirements by specified dates."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1985-65-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The delay in communicating the determination was material to overruling a delay objection in certiorari, but the statement drops that limiting procedural context."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1985-9-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court relied on the natural-person/legal-person distinction to hold that a temple could not receive property as a fideicommissary."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1985-9-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court held that references to temple property in the Buddhist Temporalities Ordinance concern sanghika property, which the disputed lands were not."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1985-9-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The trust argument was rejected because it was a mixed question of fact and law not raised in the District Court."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-21-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":false,"usable":false,"reason":"The proposition was part of the holding on an illegal tenancy, but it omits the no-certificate statutory illegality and cites section 13(2) instead of the provisions actually construed."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-22-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":false,"usable":false,"reason":"This was a fact-specific criticism supporting revision, not a legal holding, and the cited Civil Procedure Code provision was not the Code of Criminal Procedure provision construed."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-22-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":false,"usable":false,"reason":"The court found fraud on the particular police reports and facts, not a general legal rule about all public officials filing false reports, and the statute ID is wrong."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-22-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":false,"usable":false,"reason":"The covert-manoeuvre finding was a factual condemnation tied to the corrupt police assistance and null sale, while the statute ID does not match the provision construed."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-28-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court's rule was that such an apparently absolute and irrevocable Kandyan gift could still be revoked, so this statement captures only the discarded premise."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-28-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The revocability holding is correct but materially omits the statutory qualification that the right is lost if expressly renounced in the required words."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-28-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The Roman-Dutch-law point is correct, but the statement drops the court's important qualification that connected matters such as revocability remain governed by Kandyan law."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-37-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The majority held, with Jameel J. dissenting, that children adopted under the Adoption of Children Ordinance could inherit from Muslim adopting parents on intestacy."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1986-39-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":false,"usable":false,"reason":"The rei vindicatio burden rule was the holding, but it was not a construction of section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-1-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":false,"usable":false,"reason":"The co-owner point was ratio, but it omits the material warning that the decree will not bind absent co-owners and wrongly tags Civil Procedure Code section 18."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-1-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":false,"usable":false,"reason":"The burden rule was the court's holding, but it was a common-law boundary-action rule rather than a construction of Civil Procedure Code section 18."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-1-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":false,"usable":false,"reason":"The court held that title to Lot A could not be vindicated through a boundary action, but the claimed statute section was not the provision construed."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-14-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The distinction between lending money and carrying on the business of money lending was central to deciding the Money Lending Ordinance defence."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-14-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The statement is only an evidential observation about why a limited clientele did not help this plaintiff, not an independent holding."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-14-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The variety of securities was merely a factual indicator that this plaintiff was a professional money lender, not a rule of law."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-15-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court used the statutory purpose of regulating house ownership as part of its construction of the tenant-purchase scheme."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-16-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The Bank-authority question was part of the holding, but the statement omits the two other statutory questions and the finality/judicial-review distinction."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-1987-16-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The actual holding was that section 71(2) restrictions are jurisdictional and reviewable, not the vague proposition that the Finance Act restricts Bank acquisitions."}

